A host freezes the context entries it reads without a set of them.

pi-durable freezes each context entry it reads, everything in it, and
put every object it froze into one weak set for the process's life, to
skip what it had frozen before. The scheduler keeps each conversation's
range, so a host's set held every object of every live context, millions
of keys. V8 rehashes a weak table in place, on the thread: with a
million live keys one add after a collection held it 3 s, and on 19
November one held a host's thread 95 s, past its watchdog, which ended
every conversation on it. Each value frozen here is fresh from storage
or a commit, which the set never skipped, so dropping it costs only a
second walk of a head marker already frozen.

Apply only to the host's private pi build; ordinary interactive pi stays
unchanged.

